---
description: Destructive system operations require explicit confirmation
alwaysApply: true
---

# Destructive operations

Never execute `dd`, `mkfs`, `parted`, `sfdisk`, `wipefs`, `rclone sync`, `pacman -Syu`, or
`git checkout -f` against `$HOME` without quoting the exact command and receiving explicit
approval **in the current turn**. Prior approval of a similar command does not carry over.

When a command is blocked, explain why and wait for the user to approve that exact invocation.
